findings.description:
The tests are parametrized and cover each of these:
- boundary and rejection cases;
- error ordering, with declared parameters first and unknown names sorted;
- non-`str` keys;
- read-only bound mapping;
- canonical-byte equality between an omitted default and an explicit one;
- the `OutputDisplay` non-canonical guarantee;
- the "no element loops" AST guards for `confidence.py` and `labels.py`;
- the import-boundary tests for the new modules.

The fixtures the tests use (`make_series`, `make_bar_index`, `point_index`) exist in `tests/core_model/conftest.py`. The imported `CanonicalFormError` and `UNKNOWN` also exist.
